{"type":"message-part","timestamp":"2026-07-03T03:58:46.772Z","messageId":"d05601c6-1f56-45e4-ac32-e1d3e101b31d","role":"assistant","index":32,"part":{"type":"tool-attemptCompletion","toolCallId":"a2fxbpZYRdzYfSp1","state":"input-available","input":{"result":"I have successfully created the US state-level engineers choropleth visualization script and generated the required self-contained HTML file.\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n1. **Script Location**: `/home/user/myproject/build_chart.py`\n2. **Chart Output**: `/home/user/myproject/chart.html`\n3. **Libraries Used**: `altair` (v6.2.2) and `vega_datasets`\n\n### Key Features of the Visualization\n- **Data Source**: Uses `alt.topo_feature(data.us_10m.url, 'states')` to fetch TopoJSON state boundaries.\n- **Lookup Transformation**: Performs a `transform_lookup` to join state boundary shapes with the `population_engineers_hurricanes` dataset on the `id` field, retrieving the `state` name and `engineers` fields.\n- **Geographic Mark & Color**: Uses `mark_geoshape()` to render states, colored with a quantitative scale using the `\"blues\"` color scheme based on the looked-up `engineers` field.\n- **Projection**: Uses `albersUsa` projection to display the continental US, Alaska, and Hawaii correctly.\n- **Interactive Tooltip**: Displays both the `state` name and the `engineers` value on hover.\n- **Dimensions**: Set to a width of `700` and height of `400`.\n- **Export**: Saved as a self-contained HTML file using `chart.save()`.\n\n### Source Code (`build_chart.py`)\n```python\nimport altair as alt\nfrom vega_datasets import data\n\ndef main():\n    # Load US state geometries from the us-10m.json TopoJSON file\n    states = alt.topo_feature(data.us_10m.url, 'states')\n\n    # Data source URL for lookup (population, engineers, hurricanes)\n    data_url = data.population_engineers_hurricanes.url\n\n    # Build the choropleth map chart\n    chart = alt.Chart(states).mark_geoshape().encode(\n        color=alt.Color('engineers:Q', scale=alt.Scale(scheme='blues')),\n        tooltip=['state:N', 'engineers:Q']\n    ).transform_lookup(\n        lookup='id',\n        from_=alt.LookupData(data_url, key='id', fields=['state', 'engineers'])\n    ).project(\n        type='albersUsa'\n    ).properties(\n        width=700,\n        height=400\n    )\n\n    # Save the chart as a self-contained HTML file\n    chart.save('/home/user/myproject/chart.html')\n    print(\"Chart saved successfully to /home/user/myproject/chart.html\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```"},"callProviderMetadata":{"vertex":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
